    "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-financial-aid/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About A-Z Who’s Who at Trinity Directory Work at Trinity Visiting Campus Offices Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks search Assistant Director of Financial Aid Home » Jobs » Assistant Director of Financial Aid Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Assistant Director of Financial Aid Salary Range: 65k to 70k ( Salary determination is based on experience & qualifications Trinity Washington University seeks an Assistant Director of Financial Aid located in Enrollment Services. The Assistant Director of Financial Aid is responsible for managing financial aid, billing, educational financing and related services for Trinity students. In this position you will have a vital role in the management of the Federal financial programs, as well as some operations of PowerFAIDS, which is the student financial aid management system used by Trinity. The primary goal in this role is to provide comprehensive financial aid guidance, support and resources to help students achieve their educational goals at Trinity Washington University. This position will report directly to the Vice President for Enrollment Services. Education Requirements & Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree in appropriate field such as business, finance, education or public administration. 3 to 5 years of hands-on experience in a post-secondary financial aid office. Deep understanding of federal Title IV regulations, state programs, and institutional compliance standards. Proficiency with financial aid software and data systems such as PowerFAIDS. Responsibilities & Functions: Administer, maintain and reconcile the Federal Direct Student Loan Program and Federal Pell Grant programs. Stay current on all federal, state, and institutional regulations and policies. Serve as liaison with Technology Services, College Board, COD, NSLDS, and other partners in electronic data exchange. Oversee all external updates to PowerFAIDS. Responsible for transmitting and receiving all electronic data from PowerFAIDS to the U.S. Department of Education. Complete monthly reconciliation for Federal Direct Loans and Pell programs. Assist in the preparation of various office reports (e.g. FISAP, end-of-year, etc.) all related to financial aid programs. Download loan counseling and MPN data. Process all loan certifications and submit all disbursement rosters for processing. Manage and send financial aid information, requests and updates to students through PowerFAIDS. Create workflow processes to improve efficiency. Monitor and resolve data integration errors and COD errors. Download and screen all incoming ISIRs, verify selected ISIRs, resolve rejects as required. Participate in professional training workshops as required. Provide accurate and timely assistance to students, parents, faculty and staff regarding enrollment and financial aid. Work closely with other administrative offices to assist in the recruitment and retention of students. Assist with Open House, New Student Orientation, and other special campus events, as needed. Comply with confidentiality requirements as set by HIPAA, FERPA, federal, and state and local regulation. Other duties as requested by the Vice President for Enrollment Services. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong verbal and written skills to guide students and families through financial processes. Ability to manage heavy workloads, meet funding deadlines, and solve problems. Demonstrated ability to work in a team, support diverse populations, and assistant with daily administrative oversight. Working knowledge of Title IV regulations. Strong proficiency in Aid Management Software. Strong customer service and interpersonal communication skills. Familiarity with federal grants, direct loans, work-study administration, and institutional or state scholarship criteria. Strong knowledge of federal platforms. Hands-on experience with financial aid software systems such as PowerFAID. Ability to run reports, complete reconciliation processes, and utilize data to support administrative decisions. Demonstrated ability to problem-solve, and use high degree of professional judgement. Excellent time management skills in prioritizing tasks and managing multiple shifting deadlines in a high-volume, fast-paced environment. Ability to work cross-functionally in a collaborative environment with Admissions, the Registrar, etc. to support student recruitment and retention goals. High degree of discretion for handling sensitive and confidential financial records with empathy and integrity. Strong working knowledge of Microsoft office. Schedule and Work Environment: 40 hours per week minimum, including regular office hours to support the business hours of the University: 9am to 7pm. Includes regular Saturday hours 8am to 2pm. This is an all year-around, 12-month, full-time, in-person position. Ability to work efficiently with many interruptions from walk-ins, telephone inquiries and other student requests. The noise level is usually quiet. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to full-time employees to include Health, Dental & Vision insurance, Employer Paid Life and Disability benefits, 403(b) Retirement plan with employer match up to 6%, Paid Family Leave, Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and more. Qualified, interested applicants, please… Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. © 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About A-Z Who’s Who at Trinity Directory Work at Trinity Visiting Campus Offices Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"
    },
    "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/dean-of-the-school-of-nursing-and-health-professions/": {
      "title": "Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions",
      "description": "Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About A-Z Who’s Who at Trinity Directory Work at Trinity Visiting Campus Offices Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks search Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions Home » Jobs » Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions Salary Range: $160,000 to $180,000 Trinity in Washington, a comprehensive university in the nation’s capital, seeks a Dean for the School of Nursing and Health Professions (NHP).  The Dean is the chief academic and administrative leader for the school, providing strategic vision, academic oversight, and operational management for a diverse portfolio of undergraduate and graduate programs.  Enrolling about 300 students, NHP includes undergraduate programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Public Health, and Social Work, as well as graduate programs in Counseling, Occupational Therapy, and Public Health. The Dean is responsible for fostering academic excellence, supporting faculty and student success, strengthening external partnerships, and advancing the Trinity’s commitment to social justice, health equity, and community engagement. Reporting to the Provost and supervising a staff including 19 full-time faculty and 13 administrative staff as well as adjunct faculty as needed, the Dean is responsible to oversee the design and development of academic programs, ensuring that all programs meet accreditation and regulatory standards including CCNE, ACOTE, CACREP, CSWE and the D.C. Board of Nursing.  The Dean leads faculty hiring and assessment along with faculty professional development.  The Dean is responsible to manage the unit budget and to steward significant gifts and grants supporting the unit’s programs and students.  With the faculty, the Dean also builds and sustains strong partnership relationships for clinical placements and career pathways with healthcare systems, clinical agencies, community organizations and governmental partners throughout the Washington region. Candidates must present an earned doctorate in a field in which Trinity has a program including nursing, public health, counseling, occupational therapy, social work, or closely related health professions fields.  Candidates should also present an academic track record that includes (a) experience as a faculty member in a related academic program, and (b) at least 3 years of successful experience as a dean or equivalent senior academic administrator, and (c) scholarly and professional achievements supporting appointment at the most senior level.  Experience with interprofessional healthcare education is a plus.  Along with the academic credentials, candidates should also present at least three years of clinical experience in one of the major fields in Trinity’s curriculum.  Experience with the healthcare systems in the Washington region is an advantage.   Candidates must also have demonstrated success managing a diverse workforce to satisfy professional expectations and to achieve goals across all programs. Trinity Washington University is one of the nation’s historic Catholic women’s colleges, sustaining a commitment to women’s education in the daytime liberal arts programs while also offering coeducational professional and graduate programs including those in NHP.  Trinity enrolls about 2,000 students and is classified as a Predominantly Black/Hispanic Serving institution.  About half of Trinity’s students are D.C. residents; about 60% of undergraduates are Pell grantees. Position starts January 1, 2027. Candidates with the specified credentials should submit a complete c.v. along with a cover letter when applying with no more than two pages specifying alignment with these position requirements. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to full-time employees to include Health, Dental & Vision insurance, Employer Paid Life and Disability benefits, 403(b) Retirement plan with employer match up to 6%, Paid Family Leave, Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and more. Qualified, interested applicants, please… Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. © 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About A-Z Who’s Who at Trinity Directory Work at Trinity Visiting Campus Offices Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"
    },
    "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/head-athletic-trainer/": {
      "title": "Head Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Head Athletic Trainer - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About A-Z Who’s Who at Trinity Directory Work at Trinity Visiting Campus Offices Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks search Head Athletic Trainer Home » Jobs » Head Athletic Trainer Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Salary Range: 58k to 60k Trinity Washington University seeks an experienced Head Athletic Trainer. The Head Athletic Trainer is a 10-month permanent full-time position that oversees the Trinity Athletic Training/Sports Medicine program for 5 varsity teams and approximately 70 student-athletes. Duties include, but are not limited to: Ensure compliance with all college, state, and NCAA rules and regulations related to medical care for student-athletes. Act as a first responder for athletic injuries, treatment, rehabilitation, and referral of athletically injured student-athletes for physician care. Ensure that student-athletes are evaluated by their doctor on an annual basis to determine whether they are physically able to practice and compete in the intercollegiate sports program and coordinate records with the campus Student Health and Wellness Center. Communicate with coaches regarding the injury status of student-athletes and act as liaison between the Athletic Department and Student Health and Wellness Center. Oversee the purchasing and maintenance of training room supplies and equipment, and attend all home athletic events and post season games, provide coverage for team practices. Maintain up-to-date medical records for each student-athlete through an electronic medical records system, and submit an annual report at the conclusion of the academic year. Duties & Responsibilities: Evaluate, diagnose, and treat athletic injuries and medical conditions affecting student-athletes. Develop and implement injury prevention programs. Provide immediate care and emergency response for injuries during practices and games. Design and supervise rehabilitation and return-to-play protocols for injured athletes. Maintain confidential medical records and injury reports for all student-athletes using electronic health record system in coordination with the Health and Wellness Center. Coordinate pre-participation medical clearances. Ensure compliance with NCAA DIII health and safety regulations. Develop and update emergency action plans for athletic facilities. Monitor and manage athletic training supplies, equipment, and budget. Communicate student-athlete health status and participation recommendations with coaches and athletic department administrators. Develop policies and procedures to support safe athletic participation. Coordinate with campus health services and / or team physician for referral of student-athletes. Attend all Trinity sponsored sporting events. Assist with SAAC and other Departmental Programs including initiatives in the areas of mental health, and diversity and inclusion initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Thorough knowledge of conference, NCAA, NATA rules and regulations. Ability to effectively collaborate and communicate with persons of diverse cultures and language groups. Demonstrated personal and professional integrity Strong oral and written communication skills as well as computer competency and skills required. Ability to build and foster relationships, think creatively and take initiative. High attention to detail, accuracy and organizational skills. Strong interpersonal and teamwork abilities. Inquisitive nature with a desire to learn and explore new concepts.Ability to work independently to meet goals in a timely and accurate manner. Qualifications: Master’s degree required for certified athletic trainers. 3-5 years of experience intercollegiate athletic training. NATA certification. First Aid/CPR/AED Certification Required. SPECIAL LICENSES, REGISTRATION OR CERTIFICATION: NATA BOC BLS First Aid/AED/CPR Valid Driver’s License DC Athletic Trainer License Work Schedule: 40 hours a week. Working evenings and weekends may be requested. Employees are required to work in-person. Flexible scheduling is required: schedule includes evenings and weekends. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to full-time employees to include Health, Dental & Vision insurance, Employer Paid Life and Disability benefits, 403(b) Retirement plan with employer match up to 6%, Paid Family Leave, Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and more. Qualified, interested applicants, please… Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. © 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About A-Z Who’s Who at Trinity Directory Work at Trinity Visiting Campus Offices Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"
    },
    "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/laboratory-manager-and-ehs-officer/": {
      "title": "Laboratory Manager and EHS Officer",
      "description": "Laboratory Manager and EHS Officer - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About A-Z Who’s Who at Trinity Directory Work at Trinity Visiting Campus Offices Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks search Laboratory Manager and EHS Officer Home » Jobs » Laboratory Manager and EHS Officer Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Laboratory Manager and EHS Officer Annual Salary Range: 65k to 72k (Salary determination is based on experience & qualifications). Trinity Washington University seeks a Laboratory Manager and EHS Officer to support its science laboratories. Trinity, a comprehensive university that offers undergraduate programming in the sciences, seeks an individual for this full-time position available as early as September 1, 2026. Schedule: 40 hours per week, including regular office hours to support the business hours of the University. This is a year-round, 12-month position. Special Licenses, Registration or Certification: Safety License is a plus. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Biology, Biochemistry, Chemistry, or a related field Appropriate laboratory experience. Position Overview: Supporting Science faculty and supervising student workers , the Laboratory Manager will be responsible for preparing materials for teaching lab exercises, and for maintaining clean and safe labs with working equipment in Biology, Microbiology, Chemistry, Anatomy & Physiology, Forensic Science, Environmental Science, and Physics. Duties include working collaboratively with faculty to understand their course needs, training and supervising student workers, keeping inventories and planning ahead to maintain appropriate stock, purchasing, and managing financial records. Under the supervision of the Dean of the College of Arts and Sciences, the Laboratory Manager will be the first responder for issues related to equipment/instrumentation inventory, care and maintenance. The Laboratory Manager will at times be called to share their expertise through an instructional role that supports laboratory experiences for students and/or through teaching opportunities. As EHS Officer, the individual will be responsible for adherence to biohazard/chemical safety precautions, chemical waste management, inventory and disposal of biohazard materials and chemicals, database for chemical safety data sheets, safety training for faculty, students, adjuncts, safety checks and safety records, and keeping current on regulations and requirements. Essential Responsibilities: Preparing lab materials. Maintaining a clean and safe environment. Supervising student workers. Working collaboratively with faculty to understand their needs. Keeping inventory and ordering supplies as needed. Maintaining financial records. Handling chemical waste managements and disposal of waste. Keeping a database for chemical safety data sheets. Training students, faculty, adjuncts, and staff in proper use of materials. Managing safety checks and safety records. Keeping current on regulations and requirements related to the management of chemicals and safety issues. Other duties as assigned. When applying please submit a cover letter and resume. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to full-time employees to include Health, Dental & Vision insurance, Employer Paid Life and Disability benefits, 403(b) Retirement plan with employer match up to 6%, Paid Family Leave, Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and more. Qualified, interested applicants, please… Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. © 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About A-Z Who’s Who at Trinity Directory Work at Trinity Visiting Campus Offices Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"
    }
